[{:db/id 17592186147543 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-138791bc-5cad-58ca-ae3d-64015f9ea134"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147797 :question/problem "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$\\,$\n$20%$ is equivalent to \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is \n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{2}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "To convert the percent to a fraction, we first write $20%$ as a fraction with a denominator $100:$\n\n$$\n20%=\\frac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $10:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{20}{100}=\\frac{20÷10}{100÷10}=\\frac{2}{10}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{10}=\\frac{2÷2}{10÷2}=\\frac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}<\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $20%$ is equivalent to $\\frac{1}{5},$ \nwhich is $\\text{smaller than}$ $\\frac{2}{5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144530 :answer-field/correct 17592186144533 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144526 :answer-field/correct 17592186144528 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147799 :question/problem "Matt and Abraham have the same number of marbles. A total of $63%$ of Matt's marbles are blue, while $\\frac{3}{4}$ of Abraham's marbles are blue. Select the options that make the statements below true.\n\n$\\,$\nA total of \n{{field-1}}\nof Abraham's marbles are blue. \n\n$\\,$\nTherefore, he has \n{{field-2}}\nblue marbles compared to Matt." :question/worked-solution "We need to compare $\\frac{3}{4}$ with $63%.$ We can do this by writing $\\frac{3}{4}$ as a percent.\n\nFirst, we write $\\frac{3}{4}$ as an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{3\\times 25}{4\\times 25}=\\frac{75}{100}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\frac{75}{100}=75%\n$$\n\nSince $75%>63%,$ we have the following:\n\n- A total of $75%$ of Abraham's marbles are blue.\n\n- Therefore, he has $\\text{more}$ blue marbles compared to Matt." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144544 :answer-field/correct 17592186144547 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144549 :answer-field/correct 17592186144551 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147544 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-16a4ed86-6ba4-5b08-b5bc-00c64da3da49"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147801 :question/problem "Lionel and David are youth soccer players. In the previous season, $12%$ of Lionel’s goals were scored from the penalty spot, while the decimal proportion of David’s goals scored from the penalty spot was $0.1.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Lionel's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\nII. More than half of David's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\nIII. Lionel had a greater percentage of goals scored from the penalty spot compared to David." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n12%<50%,\n$$\n\nless than half of Lionel's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n0.1<0.5.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of David's goals scored were from the penalty spot.\n\n- Statement III is true. We can compare $12%$ and $0.1$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.1\\times 100=10%\n$$\n\nSince  $12%>10%,$ Lionel had a **greater** percentage of goals scored from the penalty spot compared to David.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144560 :answer-field/correct 17592186144562 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-138791bc-5cad-58ca-ae3d-64015f9ea134" :question/id #uuid "138791bc-5cad-58ca-ae3d-64015f9ea134" :question/math-academy-id "q-349678" :question/problem "Select the options that make the statement below true.\n\n$\\,$\n$45%$ is equivalent to \n{{field-1}},\nwhich is \n{{field-2}}\n$\\frac{17}{40}.$" :question/worked-solution "To convert the percent to a fraction, we first write $45%$ as a fraction with a denominator $100:$\n\n$$\n45%=\\frac{45}{100}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the fraction by dividing the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nWe can write this with a denominator of $40$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{20}=\\frac{9\\times 2}{20\\times 2}=\\frac{18}{40}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n$$\n\\frac{18}{40}>\\frac{17}{40}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ is equivalent to $\\frac{18}{40},$ \nwhich is $\\text{greater than}$ $\\frac{17}{40}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c1896846-f13a-5c11-a37a-ffc9a894ca42" "answer-field-0b435f79-e45f-54bc-a9c1-2ebc68f39df2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c1896846-f13a-5c11-a37a-ffc9a894ca42" :answer-field/id #uuid "c1896846-f13a-5c11-a37a-ffc9a894ca42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4da1f349-69e6-5209-8396-1c722ffbf3d6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-43eb7fb9-45e1-5182-81e4-f59709d8a423" "answer-355f6139-1632-5fb9-a099-f60c0204143d" "answer-4da1f349-69e6-5209-8396-1c722ffbf3d6" "answer-4e451e41-9d76-5570-9fd1-85be78bfe38d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43eb7fb9-45e1-5182-81e4-f59709d8a423" :answer/id #uuid "43eb7fb9-45e1-5182-81e4-f59709d8a423" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{16}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-355f6139-1632-5fb9-a099-f60c0204143d" :answer/id #uuid "355f6139-1632-5fb9-a099-f60c0204143d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4da1f349-69e6-5209-8396-1c722ffbf3d6" :answer/id #uuid "4da1f349-69e6-5209-8396-1c722ffbf3d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{18}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4e451e41-9d76-5570-9fd1-85be78bfe38d" :answer/id #uuid "4e451e41-9d76-5570-9fd1-85be78bfe38d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{40}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0b435f79-e45f-54bc-a9c1-2ebc68f39df2" :answer-field/id #uuid "0b435f79-e45f-54bc-a9c1-2ebc68f39df2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-cb6ea343-a5aa-5d69-b351-d0c27cab6e7f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6fc398c3-ef25-52ba-8a15-a914c2acb08b" "answer-cb6ea343-a5aa-5d69-b351-d0c27cab6e7f" "answer-f52cda3d-118c-5960-b7d2-b5e6e6485224"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6fc398c3-ef25-52ba-8a15-a914c2acb08b" :answer/id #uuid "6fc398c3-ef25-52ba-8a15-a914c2acb08b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "equal to" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb6ea343-a5aa-5d69-b351-d0c27cab6e7f" :answer/id #uuid "cb6ea343-a5aa-5d69-b351-d0c27cab6e7f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "greater than" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f52cda3d-118c-5960-b7d2-b5e6e6485224" :answer/id #uuid "f52cda3d-118c-5960-b7d2-b5e6e6485224" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "smaller than" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-16a4ed86-6ba4-5b08-b5bc-00c64da3da49" :question/id #uuid "16a4ed86-6ba4-5b08-b5bc-00c64da3da49" :question/math-academy-id "q-350266" :question/problem "Sana and Talia are students. In the previous semester, the decimal proportion of Sana’s homework assignments that were turned in early was $0.4,$ while $45%$ of Talia’s homework assignments were turned in early. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Less than half of Sana's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\nII. More than half of Talia's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\nIII. Sana had a greater percentage of homework assignments turned in early compared to Talia." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n0.4<0.5,\n$$\n\nless than half of Sana's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\n- Statement II is false. Notice that \n\n$$\n45%<50%.\n$$\n\nSo, less than half of Talia's homework assignments were turned in early.\n\n- Statement III is false. We can compare $0.4$ and $45%$ by converting the decimal into a percent. \n\nTo do this, we multiply it by $100:$\n\n$$\n0.4\\times 100=40%\n$$\n\nSince  $40%<45%,$ Sana did not have a greater percentage of homework assignments turned in early compared to Talia.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-09954eee-e3cc-5394-bd09-4440f9d978a2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-09954eee-e3cc-5394-bd09-4440f9d978a2" :answer-field/id #uuid "09954eee-e3cc-5394-bd09-4440f9d978a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c956c11a-2fd4-59e8-a085-706468c3a376" :answer-field/choices ["answer-739f06d6-c702-56c9-a051-08e032332d7a" "answer-585c654e-1a6c-5f56-ac8d-5f161ee40bff" "answer-c956c11a-2fd4-59e8-a085-706468c3a376" "answer-1129c1e9-1f22-5780-9696-b4a255e78851" "answer-9ab8acb2-0f16-5f40-8fd6-1f3209f135e3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-739f06d6-c702-56c9-a051-08e032332d7a" :answer/id #uuid "739f06d6-c702-56c9-a051-08e032332d7a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-585c654e-1a6c-5f56-ac8d-5f161ee40bff" :answer/id #uuid "585c654e-1a6c-5f56-ac8d-5f161ee40bff" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c956c11a-2fd4-59e8-a085-706468c3a376" :answer/id #uuid "c956c11a-2fd4-59e8-a085-706468c3a376" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1129c1e9-1f22-5780-9696-b4a255e78851" :answer/id #uuid "1129c1e9-1f22-5780-9696-b4a255e78851" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ab8acb2-0f16-5f40-8fd6-1f3209f135e3" :answer/id #uuid "9ab8acb2-0f16-5f40-8fd6-1f3209f135e3" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-8fdc0e2d-e98a-546b-920a-d66ad029459e" :activity/id #uuid "8fdc0e2d-e98a-546b-920a-d66ad029459e" :activity/title "Comparing Fractions, Percents, and Decimals" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049531 :activity/course 17592186046648 :activity/steps ["step-334dd9af-1647-5c57-bfb3-97a4e3ad59e7" "step-cf9b1dbf-2308-5acb-ba12-635c8825ef8b" "step-37767ed4-b4c6-547e-a639-f6aeaee3ddec" "step-63533d39-a10e-52e0-8ad1-5274656cd410" "step-e00df753-1591-526d-a3e8-f3c5207c5bfd"] :activity/first-step "step-334dd9af-1647-5c57-bfb3-97a4e3ad59e7" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-334dd9af-1647-5c57-bfb3-97a4e3ad59e7" :step/id #uuid "334dd9af-1647-5c57-bfb3-97a4e3ad59e7" :step/content 17592186147797 :step/next "step-cf9b1dbf-2308-5acb-ba12-635c8825ef8b" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cf9b1dbf-2308-5acb-ba12-635c8825ef8b" :step/id #uuid "cf9b1dbf-2308-5acb-ba12-635c8825ef8b" :step/content 17592186147799 :step/next "step-37767ed4-b4c6-547e-a639-f6aeaee3ddec" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-37767ed4-b4c6-547e-a639-f6aeaee3ddec" :step/id #uuid "37767ed4-b4c6-547e-a639-f6aeaee3ddec" :step/content 17592186147801 :step/next "step-63533d39-a10e-52e0-8ad1-5274656cd410" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-63533d39-a10e-52e0-8ad1-5274656cd410" :step/id #uuid "63533d39-a10e-52e0-8ad1-5274656cd410" :step/content "question-138791bc-5cad-58ca-ae3d-64015f9ea134" :step/next "step-e00df753-1